Hands-on Lab 1: Create an NSG
Azure Portal

Create:

Setting	Value
Name	nsg-web-dev
Resource Group	rg-az400-dev
Region	Central India
Azure CLI
az network nsg create \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --name nsg-web-dev

Verify:

az network nsg list --output table
Hands-on Lab 2: Create an HTTPS Rule
az network nsg rule create \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --nsg-name nsg-web-dev \
  --name AllowHTTPS \
  --priority 100 \
  --direction Inbound \
  --access Allow \
  --protocol Tcp \
  --destination-port-ranges 443
Hands-on Lab 3: Create an SSH Rule

Allow SSH only from your public IP.

az network nsg rule create \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --nsg-name nsg-web-dev \
  --name AllowSSH \
  --priority 110 \
  --direction Inbound \
  --access Allow \
  --protocol Tcp \
  --source-address-prefixes 115.114.88.222/32 \
  --destination-port-ranges 22

Replace <YOUR_PUBLIC_IP> with your actual public IP address.

Hands-on Lab 4: Associate NSG with a Subnet

Portal:

Open Virtual Network
Select Subnets
Choose web-subnet
Associate nsg-web-dev

CLI:

az network vnet subnet update \
  --resource-group rg-az400-dev \
  --vnet-name vnet-az400-dev \
  --name web-subnet \
  --network-security-group nsg-web-dev
