Key Takeaways
NSGs are Azure's primary network traffic filtering mechanism.
Rules are processed in priority order (lowest number first).
Subnet-level NSGs are generally preferred in enterprise environments.
ASGs simplify security rule management by grouping resources logically instead of relying on IP addresses.
Azure provides default NSG rules, but custom rules with higher precedence can override them.